import lib/ui_components.dl

class:
    patterns:
        control state
    members:
        changed as an integer

this control state means: this window's state as a pointer to control state

window control lab:
    page "menu":
        panel at 20 20 sized 240 by 320:
            switch "Grid"
            choices "Pace":
                option "Relaxed"
                option "Classic"
    page "settings":
        label "Settings"
    code:
        when the "Grid" control changes:
            increment this control state's changed
        when the "Pace" control changes:
            increment this control state's changed

set state to a new control state
set instance to an instance of control lab with state (the address of state)
show page "menu" in the address of instance
set toggle to the control labeled "Grid" in the address of instance
activate toggle belonging to control lab in the address of instance
print (the "Grid" switch is on in the address of instance) as a line
set choice to the control labeled "Pace" in the address of instance
activate (the UI child at 1 in choice) belonging to choice in the address of instance
print (the value of "Pace" in the address of instance) as a line
print state's changed as a line
show page "settings" in the address of instance
print instance's page's text as a line
close the address of instance

set {other state} to a new control state
set other to an instance of control lab with state (the address of other state)
require condition ((the "Grid" switch is on in the address of other) = false) reporting "UI instances shared control values"
require condition (other state's changed = 0) reporting "UI instances shared callback state"
close the address of other
